get_id":"81bd-0448-7ed6-4658"},{"link_uuid":"ee9d0ef5-feb5-4882-a1ec-6d35f57547b1","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c96b-bec8-ea2d-4c52"},{"link_uuid":"1416cc4f-3206-4647-aca3-278de94b35cd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c70a-1dea-f39f-446b"},{"link_uuid":"42835926-fcbd-4414-ba85-1783cc36386c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e9d9-4315-2e12-4e3c"},{"link_uuid":"45e1a72d-ebc1-4c0f-90f8-c5ee6b8357f6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"387d-e93a-36c4-41b0"},{"link_uuid":"1bcacf82-fd99-4a20-9739-a1c7d08dc43f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"d4cf-72ad-94a4-418f"},{"link_uuid":"d459f40c-c1e3-40e6-9fc4-1b46c4baecc3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"bed8-d1fc-e12d-43d7"},{"link_uuid":"7bd1eb6e-11ed-4ff2-bc3e-dfedce447730","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"45ce-8623-4a5b-464a"},{"link_uuid":"8ec187df-7fee-4ab9-bf16-11c70166f6eb","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ba9f-c9d7-0208-4ae5"},{"link_uuid":"25246f75-641c-48a8-bb1e-b6d4900c2990","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"21d5-4c6c-5478-4a9e"},{"link_uuid":"8c423240-6c24-492e-afb7-bcc2ee989aa6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"644b-6ada-6b71-4a04"},{"link_uuid":"f20afb1d-e591-47a5-9b2f-21d27f6386b8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1fae-9d2c-2855-45f5"},{"link_uuid":"4f5b7fc0-9da4-40af-9c10-01088eb24d96","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fb3e-09d7-49af-4ba7"},{"link_uuid":"f300650c-bf9e-47cd-a54d-3087a86511b7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b075-aae8-b6fc-4262"},{"link_uuid":"719d8f70-106c-4e33-827f-f6519519be7a","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0ad4-2122-f060-4a47"},{"link_uuid":"e5e2940f-7e4d-4f21-bd8b-6bdb6e77f531","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7154-b8dd-6cb9-4fe3"},{"link_uuid":"3500f06c-9ec2-4db7-be2a-2008254f1bc5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"115e-1e8d-f67e-4c7f"},{"link_uuid":"f5871ddf-223d-4554-9b9d-7fc7bae75683","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ac29-2e03-2dab-48bf"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference_mutation_verbs.py:1-10` — Preserve mutation-verb coverage in generated CLI reference. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py:1-16` — Preserve deterministic CLI-reference generation and drift detection. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py:1-25` — Preserve deterministic config-reference generation and drift detection. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:34-37, 68-73, 157-165, 169-173, 216-219, 225-240, 263-273, 284-291, 304-313` — Preserve registry generation, ordering, escaping, ownership, and drift contracts. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gerrit_hook_install.py:1-18, 93-98` — Preserve shared-hook safety and idempotent installation. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py:1-11` — Preserve actionable Verified-failure triage guidance. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew.py:1-23, 36-40` — Preserve Git-version floor evaluation against the target tree. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_git_timeout_bounds_77e1.py:1-26` — Preserve bounded Git subprocess operations. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_git_timeout_bounds_983f.py:1-24` — Preserve bounded Git subprocess operations for this regression path. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_git_version_floor.py:1-21` — Preserve supported Git-version parsing and minimum enforcement. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_gitutil_transient_write_retry.py:1-16` — Preserve bounded retry only for classified transient writes. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_guide_criterion_pins.py:1-16, 230-235` — Preserve guide-to-criterion pin integrity. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_guides.py:197-208` — Preserve packaged-guide rendering and lookup behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_header_delivery.py:166-173` — Preserve exact header delivery behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py:1-15` — Preserve complete removal of legacy HMAC op-cert support. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_264f.py:1-9` — Preserve the identity regression contract. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_2f13_heldout.py:1-7` — Preserve independent identity regression coverage. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_identity_2f13.py:1-8` — Preserve the identity regression contract. Consumer: test maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference_mutation_verbs.py tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py t